        'article' => '<h2>What are network ports?</h2><p>A port is a number (0 to 65535) that identifies, within a given IP address, which service or application should receive a connection\'s data — like an "extension" within the "phone number" that is the IP. Ports 0 to 1023 are the "well-known ports", reserved for standardized services like HTTP (80), HTTPS (443) and SSH (22).</p><h2>How to use it</h2><p>Type a port number or a service name (e.g. "ssh", "mysql", "443") to filter the table instantly.</p>',
