        'strings' => ['error' => 'Enter valid numeric values greater than zero.', 'tempoEstimado' => 'Estimated download time', 'velocidadeReal' => 'Real speed considered'],
        'article' => '<h2>Why is my download slower than my plan\'s advertised speed?</h2><p>Internet plans are advertised in <strong>megabits</strong> per second (Mbps), but file sizes are measured in <strong>megabytes</strong> (MB) — and 1 byte = 8 bits. So a "100 Meg" plan (100 Mbps) downloads at a theoretical maximum of 12.5 MB/s (100 ÷ 8), not counting network loss, bandwidth sharing and protocol overhead, which usually reduce real speed by 10-20%.</p><h2>How to use it</h2><p>Enter the file size and your connection speed (you can check this with a speed test) — the calculator estimates download time using the correct bit-to-byte conversion.</p>',
        'faq' => [
