        'strings' => ['error' => 'Enter a valid weight.', 'consumoLabel' => 'Recommended water intake', 'diaAbrev' => 'day', 'coposLabel' => 'Equivalent in glasses', 'coposNota' => '250ml glasses'],
        'article' => '<h2>The 35ml per kg rule</h2><p>This calculator uses the practical rule most cited by dietitians: roughly <strong>35ml of water per kilogram of body weight</strong> per day, as a starting point for a healthy, sedentary adult. To that base value, we add an adjustment for physical activity (sweating during exercise increases fluid replacement needs) and for hot/humid climate (which increases fluid loss through sweat even at rest).</p><h2>Does this include only plain water?</h2><p>No — the body\'s total fluid needs are also partly met by other beverages and by the water content of food (fruits and vegetables, for example, have high water content). The value calculated here is a reference for water consumed as the main beverage, not a rigid limit.</p><p><em>People with kidney, heart or other conditions requiring fluid restriction should follow specific medical guidance instead of this general estimate.</em></p>',
