            ['q' => 'Por que alguém escolheria a bola de neve, então?', 'a' => 'Porque quitar dívidas pequenas rapidamente gera uma sensação de progresso e motivação, o que ajuda muitas pessoas a manter a disciplina até o fim — mesmo pagando um pouco mais de juros no total.'],
            ['q' => 'Como informar a taxa de juros da dívida?', 'a' => 'Use a taxa de juros mensal em porcentagem. Se seu cartão cobra juros anuais, converta para uma taxa mensal aproximada antes de informar.'],
            ['q' => 'O que acontece se eu não tiver valor extra disponível?', 'a' => 'Você ainda pode comparar as duas estratégias com valor extra igual a zero — nesse caso, o resultado mostra quanto tempo levaria pagando apenas os mínimos de cada dívida.'],
        ],
    ],
    'en' => [
        'title' => 'Debt Payoff Calculator: Snowball vs. Avalanche | uToolsGo',
        'meta'  => 'Compare the snowball and avalanche strategies to pay off your debts faster. See months to payoff and total interest for each.',
        'h1'    => 'Debt Payoff Calculator (Snowball vs. Avalanche)',
        'subtitle' => 'Compare the snowball and avalanche strategies to find out which pays off your debts faster and with less interest.',
        'fieldLabels' => [
            'dividasLista' => 'Your debts (one per line: name:balance:monthly rate %:minimum payment)',
            'extraMensalDivida' => 'Extra amount available per month (beyond the minimums)',
        ],
        'fieldPlaceholders' => [
            'dividasLista' => "Credit card:3000:12:150\nCar loan:15000:1.8:450\nPersonal loan:5000:4:200",
        ],
        'strings' => [
            'monthsLabel' => 'Months to pay off everything', 'totalInterestLabel' => 'Total interest paid',
            'snowballLabel' => 'Snowball (smallest balance first)', 'avalancheLabel' => 'Avalanche (highest rate first)',
            'cheaperLabel' => 'Cheaper strategy (less interest)',
            'error' => 'Please enter at least one valid debt in the format name:balance:rate:minimum payment.',
        ],
        'article' => '<h2>How to use it</h2><p>List each debt on its own line, in the format <code>name:balance:monthly interest rate (%):minimum monthly payment</code>. For example: <code>Credit card:3000:12:150</code>. Also enter how much extra money you have available each month, beyond the minimum payments, to speed up payoff.</p><h2>The snowball strategy</h2><p>Here, you focus the extra payment on the debt with the <strong>smallest balance</strong>, paying only the minimum on the rest. Once the smallest debt is paid off, the amount that was going to it "rolls over" to the next smallest, like a snowball growing. The advantage is psychological: paying off debts quickly builds motivation to keep going.</p><h2>The avalanche strategy</h2><p>Here, the extra payment goes to the debt with the <strong>highest interest rate</strong>, regardless of balance. Mathematically, this strategy almost always results in less total interest paid and a faster overall payoff, since it tackles the most expensive debt first.</p><h2>Which one to choose</h2><p>If your goal is to save the most money on interest, avalanche usually wins. If you need quick wins to stay motivated and not give up on the plan, snowball can work better in practice, even if it costs a bit more in interest.</p>',
        'faq' => [
            ['q' => 'Which strategy saves more money?', 'a' => 'Avalanche (tackling the highest interest rate first) almost always results in less total interest paid, because it reduces the most expensive balance faster.'],
            ['q' => 'Why would anyone choose snowball, then?', 'a' => 'Because paying off small debts quickly creates a sense of progress and motivation, which helps many people stick with the plan until the end — even if it costs slightly more in total interest.'],
            ['q' => 'How do I enter the debt\'s interest rate?', 'a' => 'Use the monthly interest rate as a percentage. If your card charges an annual rate, convert it to an approximate monthly rate before entering it.'],
            ['q' => 'What if I have no extra money available?', 'a' => 'You can still compare both strategies with extra set to zero — in that case, the result shows how long it would take paying only the minimums on each debt.'],
        ],
    ],
    'es' => [
        'title' => 'Calculadora de Pago de Deudas: Bola de Nieve vs. Avalancha | uToolsGo',
        'meta'  => 'Compara las estrategias bola de nieve y avalancha para pagar tus deudas más rápido. Ve meses hasta liquidarlas y el interés total de cada una.',
        'h1'    => 'Calculadora de Pago de Deudas (Bola de Nieve vs. Avalancha)',
        'subtitle' => 'Compara las estrategias bola de nieve y avalancha para descubrir cuál liquida tus deudas más rápido y con menos intereses.',
        'fieldLabels' => [
