            'creditosTotaisLabel' => 'Total credits',
        ],
        'article' => '<h2>What is CR / IRA</h2><p>The academic performance coefficient (called CR or IRA at Brazilian universities, similar to a weighted GPA) is the student\'s average grade weighted by each course\'s credit hours. It\'s used for scholarships, exchange programs, honors and academic ranking.</p><h2>How to calculate it</h2><p><strong>CR = Σ(grade × credits) ÷ Σ(credits)</strong>. Courses with more credit hours (usually more class hours) weigh more in the calculation.</p><h2>How to use it</h2><p>Enter one course per line, formatted as <code>name:grade:credits</code>. Example: <code>Calculus I:8.5:4</code> means a grade of 8.5 in a 4-credit course.</p><h2>Differences between universities</h2><p>Each university may have its own official CR/IRA formula (some use credits, others class hours, others handle failed courses differently) — check your institution\'s official rules for the exact calculation.</p>',
        'faq' => [
