        'article' => '<h2>Why account for technical waste</h2><p>Installing flooring or tile always involves cuts and offcuts — known as technical waste. The market standard is 8% to 12%, and this calculator uses 10% as the default (adjustable).</p><h2>Formula</h2><p><strong>Boxes = ⌈(room area × (1 + waste%)) ÷ area per box⌉</strong>, always rounded up (you can\'t buy half a box).</p><h2>How to find "area per box"</h2><p>This information is on the product packaging or spec sheet, usually expressed in m²/box or sq ft/box.</p><h2>Tip</h2><p>For irregularly shaped rooms or lots of cuts (like bathrooms with many corners), consider using a higher waste factor, 12% to 15%.</p>',
