        'article' => '<h2>How to calculate the amount of mortar</h2><p>The formula is: <strong>Total kg = area × thickness (cm) × product consumption (kg/m²/cm)</strong>. Consumption depends on the mortar type — the default in this calculator (17 kg/m²/cm) is a typical average for cement render mortars; always check the specific product\'s spec sheet.</p><h2>Standard bag size</h2><p>The default bag weight here is 20 kg (a common size in the Brazilian market) — adjustable if your local supplier uses a different bag size.</p><h2>Example</h2><p>A 30 m² wall with a 2 cm render layer, consumption of 17 kg/m²/cm: 30 × 2 × 17 = 1,020 kg → 51 bags of 20 kg.</p><h2>Tip</h2><p>Always check the spec sheet of the specific mortar you\'ll buy — consumption can vary quite a bit between brands and types (render, screed, tile-setting).</p>',
        'faq' => [
