        'article' => '<h2>How the CLT hourly rate is calculated</h2><p>Unlike a freelancer, a CLT employee already has a fixed rate and hours set by contract. To find the hourly rate, the weekly hours are converted into an equivalent monthly figure and the salary is divided by it.</p><h2>Formula used</h2><p><strong>Monthly hours = (weekly hours ÷ 6) × 30</strong> — the same logic behind the official payroll divisors used in Brazil (e.g. 220h for a 44h/week schedule, the most common CLT arrangement). <strong>Hourly rate = monthly salary ÷ monthly hours</strong>.</p><h2>What it\'s useful for</h2><p>Handy for comparing your CLT hourly value against a freelance/contractor hourly proposal (see the <a href="/en/personal-finance/freelancer-rate-calculator/">freelancer rate calculator</a>, which uses a different formula since it must bake in costs and unpaid vacation time).</p>',
        'faq' => [
            ['q' => 'Why divide by 6 days instead of 7?', 'a' => 'Because the standard CLT schedule assumes 6 working days a week (accounting for the paid weekly rest day), producing the historical 220h divisor for a 44h week.'],
            ['q' => 'Is this the same math as the freelancer calculator?', 'a' => 'No. A freelancer needs to bake costs, taxes and unpaid time off into the hourly rate; a CLT employee already has those guaranteed separately, so the math here is more direct.'],
            ['q' => 'Does this include overtime?', 'a' => 'No, this is the regular hourly rate. Overtime carries a minimum 50% premium over it (100% on Sundays/holidays, unless a different agreement applies).'],
        ],
    ],
    'es' => [
        'title' => 'Calculadora de Valor de la Hora CLT (Brasil) | uToolsGo',
        'meta'  => 'Calcula cuánto vale tu hora de trabajo como empleado CLT en Brasil, a partir del salario mensual y la carga horaria semanal.',
        'h1'    => 'Calculadora de Valor de la Hora CLT',
        'subtitle' => 'Descubre el valor de tu hora de trabajo como empleado CLT en Brasil.',
        'fieldLabels' => ['monthlySalaryClt' => 'Salario mensual (R$)', 'weeklyHoursClt' => 'Carga horaria semanal (h)'],
        'strings' => [
            'error' => 'Ingresa un salario válido y una carga horaria entre 1 y 44 horas semanales.',
            'hourlyRateLabel' => 'Valor de la hora', 'monthlyHoursLabel' => 'Horas mensuales equivalentes',
        ],
        'article' => '<h2>Cómo se calcula la hora del CLT</h2><p>A diferencia de un freelancer, el empleado CLT ya tiene tarifa y jornada fijadas por contrato. Para hallar el valor de la hora, se convierte la jornada semanal en una jornada mensual equivalente y se divide el salario por ella.</p><h2>Fórmula usada</h2><p><strong>Horas mensuales = (jornada semanal ÷ 6) × 30</strong> — la misma lógica de los divisores oficiales usados en las nóminas brasileñas (ej: 220h para una jornada de 44h semanales). <strong>Valor de la hora = salario mensual ÷ horas mensuales</strong>.</p><h2>Para qué sirve</h2><p>Útil para comparar el valor de tu hora como CLT con una propuesta de hora freelance (ver la calculadora de tarifa freelance, que usa una fórmula distinta al incluir costos y vacaciones).</p>',
        'faq' => [
