            'oddsResultLabel' => 'Equivalent decimal odds', 'probResultLabel' => 'Implied probability',
        ],
        'article' => '<h2>What implied probability is</h2><p>It\'s the chance of an outcome, embedded in a market odd. Low odds imply high probability (favorite); high odds imply low probability (underdog).</p><h2>Formula</h2><p><strong>Probability (%) = 100 ÷ decimal odds</strong>. And the reverse: <strong>decimal odds = 100 ÷ probability (%)</strong>.</p><h2>Why does a bookmaker\'s market add up to over 100%?</h2><p>Because the odds offered embed the bookmaker\'s margin (the "vig" or "overround") — the sum of implied probabilities across all outcomes of a market is usually above 100%.</p>',
