            'negativeEvMsg' => 'Negative EV: mathematically, this bet tends to lose money long-run, if your probability estimate is accurate.',
        ],
        'article' => '<h2>What expected value (EV) is</h2><p>It\'s the average outcome you\'d expect from a bet if repeated infinitely, given the offered odds and the real probability (as you estimate it) of the event happening.</p><h2>Formula</h2><p><strong>EV = stake × (probability × odds − 1)</strong>. A positive EV means the bet is mathematically favorable long-run — assuming your probability estimate is accurate.</p><h2>Important notice</h2><p>This is a purely educational, mathematical tool. EV depends entirely on the quality of your probability estimate — if it\'s wrong, the calculation has no practical value. This calculator is not an encouragement to bet, and betting carries a real risk of losing money.</p>',
