        'article' => '<h2>CAC formula</h2><p><strong>CAC = Total marketing and sales spend ÷ Number of new customers acquired</strong>, over the same period.</p><h2>What to include in the spend</h2><p>Ideally, all investment that generated those customers: paid media, sales/marketing team salaries, tools, commissions — not just ad spend.</p><h2>Is a low CAC always good?</h2><p>Not on its own — CAC needs to be analyzed alongside <a href="/en/calculators/ltv-calculator/">LTV (customer lifetime value)</a>. A low CAC with an even lower LTV is still a bad business.</p>',
