        'article' => '<p>Convert your <strong>clothing size</strong> between the Brazil (BR), US, EU and UK standards, for both women\'s and men\'s clothing, including the equivalent letter size (XS/S/M/L/XL).</p><h2>How the conversion works</h2><p>Pick a gender and enter the Brazilian number size (for example 40 for women\'s or 42 for men\'s) and the tool shows the matching letter size and the equivalent US, EU and UK numbers.</p><h2>Reference table — women\'s clothing</h2><table><tr><th>BR</th><th>Letter</th><th>US</th><th>EU</th><th>UK</th></tr><tr><td>34</td><td>XS</td><td>2</td><td>34</td><td>6</td></tr><tr><td>36</td><td>S</td><td>4</td><td>36</td><td>8</td></tr><tr><td>38</td><td>M</td><td>6</td><td>38</td><td>10</td></tr><tr><td>40</td><td>M/L</td><td>8</td><td>40</td><td>12</td></tr><tr><td>42</td><td>L</td><td>10</td><td>42</td><td>14</td></tr><tr><td>44</td><td>XL</td><td>12</td><td>44</td><td>16</td></tr><tr><td>46</td><td>XL</td><td>14</td><td>46</td><td>18</td></tr><tr><td>48</td><td>XXL</td><td>16</td><td>48</td><td>20</td></tr><tr><td>50</td><td>XXL</td><td>18</td><td>50</td><td>22</td></tr><tr><td>52</td><td>XXXL</td><td>20</td><td>52</td><td>24</td></tr></table><h2>Reference table — men\'s clothing</h2><table><tr><th>BR</th><th>Letter</th><th>US</th><th>EU</th><th>UK</th></tr><tr><td>36</td><td>XS</td><td>XS</td><td>44</td><td>34</td></tr><tr><td>38</td><td>S</td><td>S</td><td>46</td><td>36</td></tr><tr><td>40</td><td>M</td><td>M</td><td>48</td><td>38</td></tr><tr><td>42</td><td>M/L</td><td>M/L</td><td>50</td><td>40</td></tr><tr><td>44</td><td>L</td><td>L</td><td>52</td><td>42</td></tr><tr><td>46</td><td>XL</td><td>XL</td><td>54</td><td>44</td></tr><tr><td>48</td><td>XXL</td><td>XXL</td><td>56</td><td>46</td></tr><tr><td>50</td><td>XXL</td><td>XXL</td><td>58</td><td>48</td></tr><tr><td>52</td><td>XXXL</td><td>XXXL</td><td>60</td><td>50</td></tr></table><h2>Why sizes vary between brands</h2><p>Unlike shoes, clothing does not follow one single international standard — every brand defines its own fit (regular, slim, plus size, etc.), so the same BR number can fit differently depending on the label. Use this conversion as a starting point and always check the store\'s own measurement chart (bust, waist, hip) when available.</p><h2>Chinese sizes (Shein, Shopee, AliExpress)</h2><p>Sellers in China use two formats: the <strong>Asian label</strong> in letters (S, M, L, XL, XXL, 3XL...) and the <strong>standard Chinese code (GB/T)</strong>, written as height/bust plus a body-type letter. For example, <code>165/88A</code> means 165 cm height, 88 cm bust (or chest) and body type A (standard). The tool shows the code matching your size and suggests which letter to pick on Asian stores.</p><table><tr><th>Letter</th><th>Women</th><th>Men</th></tr><tr><td>S</td><td>155/80A</td><td>165/84A</td></tr><tr><td>M</td><td>160/84A</td><td>170/88A</td></tr><tr><td>L</td><td>165/88A</td><td>175/92A</td></tr><tr><td>XL</td><td>170/92A</td><td>180/96A</td></tr><tr><td>XXL</td><td>175/96A</td><td>185/100A</td></tr><tr><td>3XL</td><td>—</td><td>190/104A</td></tr></table><p>How a Brazilian size is matched to a code: we use the EU equivalent from the table above and pick the code whose EU size range contains yours (the smaller one when it fits two). Above XXL (women) and 3XL (men) there is no verified standard code, so the tool does not show one.</p><h2>Why go up 1 or 2 sizes</h2><p>Marketplace items with Asian labels usually fit 1 to 2 sizes smaller than the equivalent Brazilian or European size. That is why the suggestion for Shein, Shopee and AliExpress goes up 1 to 2 letter sizes. It is a rule of thumb: what matters is the listing\'s own measurement chart (bust, waist, hip) compared with your measurements.</p>',
        'faq' => [
            ['q' => 'Is Brazilian M the same as US M?', 'a' => 'Not exactly — Brazilian M (BR 38-40 women\'s) roughly maps to US 6-8, but fit varies by brand, so always check the specific size chart when possible.'],
            ['q' => 'Does this conversion apply to every brand?', 'a' => 'It is a general reference widely used in retail, but specific brands — especially international or niche ones — may use their own charts.'],
            ['q' => 'What if my size is not on the table?', 'a' => 'The tool uses the closest available table size and flags it as an approximation.'],
            ['q' => 'Are Chinese sizes smaller than Brazilian ones?', 'a' => 'Usually yes: items with Asian labels tend to fit 1 to 2 sizes smaller. Compare your measurements with the listing\'s chart instead of relying on the letter alone.'],
        ],
    ],
    'es' => [
        'title' => 'Conversor de Talla de Ropa BR, US, EU, UK Gratis | uToolsGo',
