        'article' => '<h2>How it works</h2><p>Enter any year and this calculator instantly shows the 7 official Mexican holidays under Article 74 of the Federal Labor Law — including the three holidays observed on the Monday closest to their commemorative date — entirely in your browser.</p><h2>Fixed holidays and "floating Monday" holidays</h2><p>New Year\'s Day (January 1st), Labor Day (May 1st), Independence Day (September 16th) and Christmas Day (December 25th) always fall on the same date. Constitution Day, Benito Juárez\'s Birthday and Revolution Day, on the other hand, are observed on the Monday closest to their commemorative date (February 5th, March 21st and November 20th respectively), so their exact date shifts every year.</p><h2>Already have dedicated pages for upcoming years</h2><p>If you\'re looking for 2025–2030 specifically, we have dedicated pages with the full table and extra context: <a href="/es/feriados-y-calendario/dias-feriados-oficiales-mexico-2025/">2025</a>, <a href="/es/feriados-y-calendario/dias-feriados-oficiales-mexico-2026/">2026</a>, <a href="/es/feriados-y-calendario/dias-feriados-oficiales-mexico-2027/">2027</a>, <a href="/es/feriados-y-calendario/dias-feriados-oficiales-mexico-2028/">2028</a>, <a href="/es/feriados-y-calendario/dias-feriados-oficiales-mexico-2029/">2029</a> and <a href="/es/feriados-y-calendario/dias-feriados-oficiales-mexico-2030/">2030</a>. For any other year, use the calculator above.</p>',
