            'inputPlaceholder' => 'Start typing the sample text here...',
            'timeLabel' => 'Time',
            'wpmLabel' => 'WPM',
            'accuracyLabel' => 'Accuracy',
            'restartBtn' => 'Restart test',
        ],
        'article' => '<h2>What it\'s for</h2><p>This test measures your typing speed in words per minute (WPM) and your accuracy (% of correct characters), based on an English sample text. The timer starts automatically on your first keystroke and stops when you finish typing the whole text.</p><h2>How WPM is calculated</h2><p>We use the standard typing-test industry convention, where <strong>1 "word" = 5 typed characters (including spaces)</strong>, rather than a literal count of space-separated words. This convention exists because real words vary a lot in length — counting characters gives a more consistent measure across typists. The formula is: <code>WPM = (characters typed ÷ 5) ÷ minutes elapsed</code>.</p><h2>How accuracy is calculated</h2><p>Accuracy compares, character by character, what you typed against the sample text at the same position. The result is the percentage of characters that are correct out of the total typed.</p><h2>Tips to improve</h2><p>Typing without looking at the keyboard (touch typing), keeping your fingers on the home row, and practicing regularly in short sessions tend to improve both speed and accuracy over time.</p>',
